I thought it takes a while to dig down - unless you have a _lot_ of
digging shots, you'll spend a few turns on every level, resulting in
the occasional (deadly) encounter. 

And is this, on the whole, an actual problem? Do DfVers _really_
deplete the bones repository on game installations with few users?
Since a single installation can't have multiple bones files for the
same level, this should be a non-problem for true multi-user
installations (get restocked at sufficient speed) and for single
users, well, it's their own fault.

And of course, you can harvest a large number of bones files in a
normal game, too, and only leave (at most) one. DfVers have a good
shot at nuking lots of bones files, fast, but i'm not sure it's an
actual problem in need of adressing.

